<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB3-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB3-001" ;
  triage:title "Procedure docs are generator boilerplate: fabricated Steps tables and byte-identical revision sections" ;
  triage:description "fenix critical review B1 (PR #1436 comment 5648097377, 2026-09-12T19:14:53Z) + quality-mgr QA1-B1/QA1-B2 (BB3-QA1-1789239618, 2026-09-12T19:19:46Z), reviewed at 27e21224c. scripts/procedures/inventory_reports.py:107-175 (write_procedure_docs / _report_step_names) emits all 18 docs/procedures/*.md from one hard-coded 3-node flowchart reused for the body and every revision section; step rows are the alphabetised union of cases[].name from committed evidence, or a hard-coded fallback (doctor / advertised host / smoke case results) when no evidence JSON matches -- confirmed verbatim in at least 5 docs. smoke-thorough.md shows 3 rows against the runner's 35 add_case calls; smoke-localhost.md order is alphabetical, not runner order; colima-hermes-skills.md has 48 rows vs 45 cases. Every `## Revision <rev8>` block for a given procedure is byte-identical (same Flow diagram, same Steps table) regardless of which historical revision it names, with generic revision notes (\"current\" / \"historical runner revision\"). Violates D1's requirement that Steps rows come from the runner's real per-case names in runner order, and that each revision section be authored from `git show <rev>:<runner>`. AC2 fails." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "scripts/procedures/inventory_reports.py" ;
  triage:status "fixed_partial" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T19:14:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Routed to cipher's BB3-FIX-R1 fix round (fenix, 2026-09-12T19:14:54Z; quality-mgr routing correction, 2026-09-12T19:20:54Z). Fix must include real per-case step derivation in runner order (no generic fallback) and genuine per-revision content diffing authored from git show <rev>:<runner>. Core fabrication mechanism (hardcoded flowchart + generic fallback) confirmed gone in BB3-QA2 (ruthless-boundary-qa); severity downgraded blocking to important to match the residual scope: colima-hermes-skills.md's front-matter rev (6040ecf36...) disagrees with its own body-stamped rev (9b59af6e, mermaid diagram + all 48 Steps rows) -- QA-2 finding I2, ruthless-boundary-qa RBQA-BB3-001-R1. Other 17 procedure docs should be spot-checked for the same drift. Routed to cipher's BB3-FIX-R2." ;
  triage:relatedFinding "BB3-005" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T19:14:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB3-001/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

